    "body": "Kia’s 7-seat PV5 electric van is now eligible for the UK Government’s Electric Car Grant (ECG), bringing the starting price down to £35,495 ($47,000).\nKia PV5 7-seat gains ECG eligibility\nThe PV5, Kia’s first dedicated electric van, has been a huge success. It’s primarily sold in two body types: Cargo for commercial use and Passenger, designed as an everyday family hauler.\nIn June, Kia launched the PV5 Passenger 7-seat , adding a third row. The new 2-2-3 seating arrangement opens up best-in-class legroom of up to 1,732 mm, headroom of up to 1,075 mm, and shoulder room of up to 1,732 mm.\nAfter opening orders for the 2027 PV5, Kia said all 5-seat variants were eligible for a £1,500 Government Electric Car Grant (ECG), but it would announce eligibility for the 7-seater shortly.\nAdvertisement - scroll for more content\nKia confirmed on Friday that all grades of the PV5 Passenger 7-seater are also eligible for a £1,500 ECG.\nIncluding the grant, Kia’s 7-seat electric people mover now starts at just £35,495 ($47,000), on-the-road (OTR).\nKia PV5 Passenger 7-seat variant with Elite grade interior (Source: Kia UK)\nThe 7-seat electric van is available exclusively with the long-range 71.2 kWh battery in the UK, providing up to 246 miles of WLTP range.\nWith DC fast charging of up to 150 kW, the vehicle’s battery can recharge from 10% to 80% in under 30 minutes.\nAll Kia PV5 variants, including the Cargo and Passenger, are available to order through Kia PBV centers across the UK. You can learn more and find Kia PBVs near you on Kia’s UK website .\nKia offers a full lineup of electric cars in the UK, including the new EV2, EV3, EV4, and PV5 Passenger, all eligible for the ECG.\nPV5 Passenger 7-seat | Battery | Starting Price OTR | ECG | OTR including ECG\nEssential LR HP | 71.2 kWh | £36,995 ($49,000) | £1,500 | £35,495 ($47,000)\nPlus LR HP | 71.2 kWh | £40,275 ($53,000) | £1,500 | £38,775 (51,500)\nElite LR HP | 71.2 kWh | £41,975 ($55,500) | £1,500 | £40,475 ($53,500)\n2027 Kia PV5 Passenger 7-seat prices and driving range in the UK ( SR = Standard Range 51.5kWh; LR = Long Range 71.2kWh; HP = Heat Pump )\nWith an electric vehicle in nearly every segment, Kia became “Europe’s fastest-growing top 10 passenger-car brand YTD” through August. Between January and August 2026, Kia registered 377,078 vehicles, up 9% from the same period last year.\nIn the UK, Kia is the second-best-selling electric car brand, behind only Tesla, through the first nine months of 2026.\nNext year, Kia will launch the PV7 ( check it out here ), a larger electric van with enough space for nine passengers.\nFTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links. More.\nStay up to date with the latest content by subscribing to Electrek on Google News . You’re reading Electrek— experts who break news about Tesla , electric vehicles, and green energy , day after day. Be sure to check out our homepage for all the latest news, and follow Electrek on Twitter , Facebook , and LinkedIn to stay in the loop. Don’t know where to start? Check out our YouTube channel for the latest reviews.",
